     EXPLANATION OF OPTION
 
     You can always view the current drive statuses in ace because 
     they are always displayed in the drive matrix.  Note that the 
     location of the array controller(s) is also displayed in the 
     drive matrix with a status of 7.
 
     An abbreviated meaning of each drive status is always displayed 
     in the lower left-hand corner of the drive window and labeled 
     STATUS.  For descriptions of each drive status, see the table 
     below.  
     +===============================================================+
     |  DRIVE STATUS    |              DESCRIPTION                   |
     +------------------+--------------------------------------------+
     | 0 - Optimal      | The drive is operating at an optimal level.|
     +------------------+--------------------------------------------+
     | 1 - Non-existent | No drive is physically connected to the    |
     |                  | array.                                     |
     +------------------+--------------------------------------------+
     | 2 - Spare        | The drive is connected to the array, but   |
     |                  | not configured into a logical unit.        |
     +======================= (CONTINUED) ===========================+
 
     +===============================================================+
     |  DRIVE STATUS    |              DESCRIPTION                   |
     +------------------+--------------------------------------------+
     | 3 - Failed       | The drive was failed by the array          |
     |                  | controller or by the user and must be      | 
     |                  | replaced.                                  |
     +------------------+--------------------------------------------+
     | 4 - Replaced     | The drive has just been replaced, is       |
     |                  | being formatted, or is being reconstructed.|
     +------------------+--------------------------------------------+
     | 5 - Warning      | An unrecoverable read error occurred which |
     |                  | requires you to (1) fail the drive, and    |
     |                  | (2) replace the drive, and (3) restore the | 
     |                  | logical unit.                              |
     +------------------+--------------------------------------------+
     | 6 - Mismatch     | The array controller sensed that the drive |
     |                  | has either a sector size, capacity, serial |
     |                  | number, SCSI Channel, or ID different than |
     |                  | what the array controller expected.        |
     +===============================================================+
                                (CONTINUED)
 
     +===============================================================+
     |  DRIVE STATUS    |              DESCRIPTION                   |
     +------------------+--------------------------------------------+
     | 7 - Controller   | This status is NOT a drive status - it     |
     |                  | indicates the location of the array        |
     |                  | controller in the array.                   |
     +------------------+--------------------------------------------+
     | 8 - Formatting   | The drive is currently being formatted.    |
     +------------------+--------------------------------------------+
     | 9 - Wrong drive  | The wrong drive was replaced.              |
     +===============================================================+
